# UI And Human Intuition

## SPA only
- No full-page reloads for internal navigation or state updates.
- Async work must have visible loading and actionable error states.

## GhostDASH operator model
- A first-time operator should be able to quickly find Agents, Data Sources, Connections, Logs, and chat.
- Labels should use real operator language and clear verbs.

## No duplicated settings surfaces
- Never make the same setting editable in multiple screens.
- If a value appears in multiple places, exactly one location is the editor and the rest are summaries.

## Boundaries
- The UI may call `/api/*` for operator control and `/agent/*` for chat only.
- The browser must never call providers, Qdrant, or third-party tools directly.

## Human QA before done
- Validate the changed flows from a cold start.
- Check responsive layout, error paths, save feedback, and consistency of labels/defaults.
